{"name":"Empire Rose","hex":"#e7c5c1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"empire","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A political state, often a monarchy, that has achieved a much greater current size than its initial size by conquering surrounding territories, cities or nations.","A political unit ruled by an emperor or empress."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative letter-case form of Empire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/empire"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Empire Rose","blocks":[{"text":"Empire Rose (1982–2002) was one of the most popular Thoroughbred mares to race in New Zealand and Australia. She was a gigantic chestnut, only just fitting into the barrier stalls in Melbourne."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire_Rose"},{"title":"Empire","blocks":[{"text":"An empire is a group of territories controlled by a monarch or a supreme central authority. Within an empire, different populations may have different sets of rights and may be governed differently. The word \"empire\" derives from the Roman concept of Imperium, which refers to the right to command. Empires have taken many forms throughout history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Modern_Empires.svg/330px-Modern_Empires.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Empire"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg/500px-CUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg/1280px-CUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/CUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg/500px-CUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Meeting between Spartan king Agesilaus (left) and Pharnabazus II (right).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACUH_Agesilaus_and_Pharnabazus.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Rosa_Precious_platinum.jpg/500px-Rosa_Precious_platinum.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3a/Rosa_P